@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: turn 21 has a prep decision the tutorial must freeze and teach, then hand back to the live clock
' status: proposed 2026-09-17, not implemented; _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
' would touch: not in this tree — no turn-21 prep, tutorial freeze, or siege
'   clock types exist under the sandbox checkout (measured 2026-09-17). Locate
'   the owning tutorial module before a covers: line can be honest.
'   the runner this beat sits in ........ _spec/_plans/tutorial-interactive-siege.puml
'   the draw bug it must not resemble ... _spec/_plans/turn-45-draw-stop.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT THE LINE ITEM SETTLES ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' "turn 21 prep" is a DATED BEAT. At turn 21 the live game asks for a prep
' choice (what that choice is: unmeasured). The tutorial must stop on that
' turn, make the decision visible, and resume without skipping the tax.
'
' ── WHAT IT DOES NOT SETTLE ────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   what "prep" spends or places at 21
'   whether 21 is 0-based, 1-based, or a named phase
'   whether this beat is siege-only
'
' A freeze that never resumes is the turn-45 stop in tutorial clothes. The
' clock has to start again after the choice, on turn 21's remaining work, not
' on turn 22 invented by the freeze.
title PLANNED — freeze on turn 21, teach the prep,\nhand the same turn back to the clock

component "live turn 21" as T21 <<app>>
component "prep decision" as PREP <<app>>
component "tutorial freeze + copy" as TEACH <<app>>
component "resume same turn" as RES <<app>>
component "**clock jumps to 22**\nor never starts again" as SKIP <<error>>
component "turn-45 stop (unrelated)" as T45 <<error>>

T21 ARROW_MAIN PREP
PREP ARROW_MAIN TEACH
TEACH ARROW_MAIN RES
RES ARROW_MAIN T21 : remaining work
TEACH ARROW_ERROR SKIP
SKIP ARROW_ERROR T45 : same shape, later

note bottom of TEACH
  **The beat must exhibit the preparation levy and
  then collect it as a legal engine action.** A
  tooltip over a running clock is not preparation,
  because it never submits that cost.
end note

note bottom of SKIP
  **Resume is the difficult half, because ending
  the freeze on turn twenty-two skips the
  preparation levy.** Never resuming produces a
  hung game, and both outcomes fail this item.
end note

note right of T21
  **Measure turn twenty-one in the live engine
  before authoring tutorial copy.** If ordinary
  play has no preparation on that turn, this beat
  would teach an invented house rule.
end note

legend bottom
  **The order to do it in**
  ==
  **1. Find the live hook.** What the engine does at turn 21 in a real siege
  (and in a real non-siege). If nothing, the number in the backlog is a
  content cue — do not invent a prep phase to match the title.
  --
  **2. Freeze only that decision.** Disable other verbs, keep the board, keep
  the turn index. Submit the prep as a legal engine action.
  ==
  **3. Resume the same turn.** Remaining movement, clocks, and siege lines
  continue as if the player had paused. Add a test that the turn counter is
  still 21.
  --
  **Left open**: copy; whether prep can be undone; siege-only vs all modes.
end legend
@enduml
